 - Fibonacci's checkable maximum is 78: that is the last size whose reference answer is still exactly representable in the interpreter's `f64` numbers. Larger sizes are refused with `SizeTooLarge` before the expected answer can round or reach infinity and pass `inf == inf`.
 - The 60-second budget bounds how long the harness waits, not how long the workload runs. `run_all` spends that one budget across all four workloads rather than granting each a fresh 60 seconds. The interpreter has no cancellation hook, so a timed-out worker thread is detached and may keep consuming CPU until the test process exits. In the CLI this is masked by `std::process::exit`; a future harness can run measurements in a child process if it needs a hard kill.
 - The full gate was run without any index workaround during this resumed attempt. The prior attempt's `GIT_INDEX_FILE` bullet is no longer applicable: the resumed change modifies tracked files under `tests/`, so the diff, must_touch and test-policy checks see it directly.
 - The second review round added a direct `--compare` CLI test, made the comparison loop spend one shared budget instead of a fresh 60 seconds per row, made the baseline parser refuse unknown-workload rows with a numeric size and duplicate `(workload, size)` rows, and kept the timing artifact inside the output directory when the output path is a directory. The write-failure test now proves the timing write stayed in its sandbox and the failure came from the baseline path.
+- This resumed run changed only `tests/bench_test.rs`: the preserved harness was already in `HEAD`, so `verify.sh` saw an empty diff and failed its must_touch and test-quota checks. Four new tests now pin previously untested branches (character-safe truncation, header-only baseline parsing, negative/unknown size-check refusal, and timing-artifact placement) and supply the required `edge_*` and failure-asserting coverage. No production code changed because the preserved implementation already meets the phase goal; there was no defect to fix, only coverage to add.

